      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is already remapped (`gr`, 1°), so its \"native\" numbers are on its 1° archive grid with a regridded mask. CESM2 and MPI are `gn` (100 km and 250 km), so coastal and boundary-current features are not comparable in amplitude.",
        "Moving vertical coordinates mean time-dependent volume, which matters for the volume weights."
      ]
